error[E0277]: `&mut u64` can't be given to a call as an `#[output]` of type `u64`
  --> tests/ui/output_arg_wrong_type.rs:14:10
   |
14 |     give(&mut &mut *output);
   |     ---- ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ expected `&mut u64` (or a view of one) whose contents accept every bit pattern
   |     |
   |     required by a bound introduced by this call
   |
   = help: the trait `OutputArg<u64>` is not implemented for `&mut u64`
   = note: a failed call can leave invalid contents behind, so only memory whose contents accept every bit pattern can be given to a call directly
note: required by a bound in `give`
  --> tests/ui/output_arg_wrong_type.rs:8:13
   |
 6 | fn give<Output>(_output: &mut Output)
   |    ---- required by a bound in this function
 7 | where
 8 |     Output: OutputArg<u64>,
   |             ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `give`
help: consider removing the leading `&`-reference
   |
14 -     give(&mut &mut *output);
14 +     give(&mut *output);
   |

